# At home in Russian: на ку́хне
subtitle: "The rooms and furniture of a Russian flat, на ку́хне and в спа́льне, and the three verbs for where things are: стои́т, лежи́т, виси́т."
tags: ["russian","russian home vocabulary","rooms and furniture","стоит лежит висит","на кухне"]
teaches: ["vocabulary/home","grammar/place-ending"]
thumb: "band \"Your sofa STANDS\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Cooking in Russian: вари́ть, ре́зать","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/73-russian-cooking.cast"}

